WEBVTT

00:06.970 --> 00:07.960
Sleepy...

00:08.570 --> 00:10.290
<i>All of a sudden, Usagi-san...</i>

00:12.010 --> 00:13.290
I'm going abroad!

00:13.630 --> 00:15.880
Stop this, Sensei!!

00:16.090 --> 00:19.080
How many days do you think are left before the deadline?

00:19.320 --> 00:21.790
Shut up! I know that already!

00:22.270 --> 00:24.750
Ah, Aikawa-san, good morning.

00:25.040 --> 00:26.120
What's the matter?

00:26.340 --> 00:28.690
Oh, Misaki-kun! Stop him somehow!!

00:28.740 --> 00:33.680
There's a scene in the book he's currently working on where the college student protagonist goes on a date.

00:33.740 --> 00:38.930
I told him that an ordinary date is fine, but he says he doesn't know what an ordinary date is and that it's impossible.

00:39.320 --> 00:42.380
And now he's saying he's going abroad since he can't write it!!

00:42.530 --> 00:43.350
Oh...

00:43.350 --> 00:46.810
Just 20-30 pages and it'll be done. Just write something!

00:47.010 --> 00:49.220
I'm saying, just write however you like!

00:49.260 --> 00:51.440
And who rejected it when I wrote however I liked?

00:51.790 --> 00:54.420
Ordinary college students won't make reservations at a 5 star hotels!

00:54.420 --> 00:56.940
They won't sail around the world in luxury cruise ships!

00:56.940 --> 00:58.490
And won't charter private planes!!

00:58.600 --> 00:59.340
I did.

00:59.690 --> 01:01.180
You're not ordinary!

01:01.620 --> 01:03.380
Ohh!! What do I do!!!!

01:03.380 --> 01:07.320
I won't be able to make it to the proof readers, this time! Just what lies should I feed to the printers!!

01:07.720 --> 01:08.700
The trains stopped working?

01:08.700 --> 01:10.350
My pet cat spoke and told me not to?

01:10.470 --> 01:11.950
I came down with water on the knee?

01:12.130 --> 01:18.500
Um, t-then, why don't you just tell him about your dates from when you were in college?

01:21.120 --> 01:23.530
Eh? Did I just say something strange!?

01:23.750 --> 01:25.630
Don't corner her any further.

01:25.800 --> 01:27.890
Bad, bad, bad, bad, this is really bad!!

01:27.890 --> 01:31.380
We've already sold the ads! I'll have to bear the loses if we push back the release dates now!

01:31.380 --> 01:36.100
He probably doesn't give a damn about that, but it would be a heinous disgrace for me!

01:36.100 --> 01:39.480
Isn't there a real, ordinary college student somewhere nearby!?

01:39.650 --> 01:42.160
Someone with real-life experiences we could use for material!

01:41.100 --> 01:42.680
Another BL novel?

01:42.260 --> 01:46.760
College student, college student, college student, college student, college student...

01:42.960 --> 01:45.210
Nope. This one's a normal novel.

01:45.290 --> 01:46.210
What's it about?

01:46.420 --> 01:52.070
A sensitive comedy story of young men and women's messy love with a full fledged gourmet food and onsen mystery.

01:52.920 --> 01:53.950
Oh!

01:54.300 --> 01:58.250
You're planning to put it all together in an a tale of youth for the youth, right?

01:58.390 --> 02:01.770
Ha!! Found one!! An ordinary college student!!

02:02.310 --> 02:04.980
Misaki-kun, you must be having the experience of going on an ordinary date, right?

02:05.220 --> 02:06.480
Please help!

02:06.700 --> 02:10.000
You have got to teach him about what an ordinary date is like!

02:10.090 --> 02:12.540
No... Um... I...!

02:12.650 --> 02:14.470
All of his dates have already-

02:17.540 --> 02:19.530
Ha ha! As you wish!

02:19.770 --> 02:23.480
Even though I look like this, I'm so popular with the ladies that it's troublesome!

02:23.700 --> 02:24.240
Hah!

02:26.030 --> 02:28.600
Is that so!! That'll really help!!

02:28.600 --> 02:30.480
I'll bring some Kuma cream puffs for you next time!

02:30.670 --> 02:32.020
Leave it to me!

02:32.020 --> 02:33.820
This is a piece of cake!

02:37.830 --> 02:39.220
<i>Bad, this is bad!</i>

02:39.330 --> 02:43.370
<i>Somehow I just got dragged into this mess that I can't get out of, isn't it?</i>

02:44.030 --> 02:48.970
Out of one problem and into another

02:49.300 --> 02:54.550
Afuredashita shoudou ga bokura no mune wo ustu

02:49.300 --> 02:54.550
An overflowing urge moves our hearts

02:52.250 --> 03:05.520
Junjou Romantica 2

02:54.550 --> 02:58.020
ima futari no story

02:54.550 --> 02:58.020
Now, our story...

02:59.310 --> 03:06.800
bokura no mirai ga kagayaite yuku yo

02:59.310 --> 03:06.800
Our future is going to shine on.

03:10.240 --> 03:15.530
mae ni susumeba dareka to butsukatte

03:10.240 --> 03:15.530
If I try to move forward, I collide with someone else,

03:16.000 --> 03:20.360
okubyou ni naru bakari

03:16.000 --> 03:20.360
and always lose my nerve.

03:20.360 --> 03:25.960
dakedo mae wo muite aruite iku yo

03:20.360 --> 03:25.960
But I'm going to face front and walk ahead,

03:25.960 --> 03:29.590
kimi to aeru nara

03:25.960 --> 03:29.590
if it means I can see you.

03:31.620 --> 03:36.600
ame ni utarete furueru koe

03:31.620 --> 03:36.600
Your trembling voice, pelted by the rain,

03:36.930 --> 03:42.200
nemurenu yoru wo samayottemo

03:36.930 --> 03:42.200
even if I have to wander sleepless nights,

03:42.880 --> 03:45.680
boku wa yuku yo

03:42.880 --> 03:45.680
I'll go,

03:45.680 --> 03:52.430
kimi to deaeru sono hima de

03:45.680 --> 03:52.430
Until the day when I can see you.

03:53.250 --> 03:58.440
Afuredashita shoudou ga bokura no mune wo ustu

03:53.250 --> 03:58.440
An overflowing urge moves our hearts

03:58.440 --> 04:02.150
ima futari no story

03:58.440 --> 04:02.150
Now, our story

04:02.310 --> 04:03.960
ugokidashita

04:02.310 --> 04:03.960
has started.

04:03.960 --> 04:08.950
meguriatta shougeki de iro no nai sekai ga

04:03.960 --> 04:08.950
The impact of our meeting, shocked this dull, grey world

04:08.950 --> 04:16.140
isshun de azayaka ni irozuite yuku yo

04:08.950 --> 04:16.140
and instantly burst into a brilliant color.

04:19.240 --> 04:20.940
Magazine: Special Tokyo- Tokyo's 100 Best Kept Secrets

04:21.990 --> 04:23.440
This is difficult...

04:23.650 --> 04:27.620
<i>It seems like the big deal here isn't that it has to do something with Usagi-san's book,</i>

04:27.620 --> 04:30.520
<i>but that this is some sort of a test of my manhood.</i>

04:31.880 --> 04:35.730
<i>And what's with a lack of my experience anyway?</i>

04:36.020 --> 04:38.460
Route

04:36.020 --> 04:38.460
1) Lunch in the park (a homemade bento might be good)

04:36.020 --> 04:38.460
2) Shopping (buy her something)

04:36.020 --> 04:38.460
3) Aquarium

04:36.020 --> 04:38.460
4) Ferris Wheel

04:36.020 --> 04:38.460
5) Dinner (at some nice friendly diner)

04:36.020 --> 04:38.460
6) Take her home

04:37.130 --> 04:38.720
Alright! This is perfect!

04:38.800 --> 04:39.880
Wonderful!

04:39.970 --> 04:44.700
Sure, it's more than a little clichéd, but at least with a cliché, you can't go wrong!

04:45.640 --> 04:49.510
<i>But, I'm sure Usagi-san would be really happy with this.</i>

04:50.230 --> 04:51.730
<i>Whoa! Hold it! That's not the point!</i>

04:52.110 --> 04:55.120
<i>I'm trying to show Usagi-san what I'd do on a date with a girl!</i>

04:55.200 --> 04:57.420
<i>Not what I'd do on a date with Usagi-san!</i>

04:58.530 --> 05:00.210
Such an obviously clichéd course.

05:00.390 --> 05:01.510
Don't look at it as you please!

05:01.580 --> 05:05.950
Besides, if you have this much free time to mock me, just get back to work!

05:06.800 --> 05:10.180
But you thought of all sorts of things for my sake, right?

05:13.270 --> 05:18.180
Well, sort of. Aikawa-san looked like she was about to drop dead from stress and overwork.

05:18.530 --> 05:20.760
What do we do about the dinner of no. 5?

05:21.030 --> 05:22.600
Japanese food? French?

05:22.650 --> 05:23.570
A family restaurant!

05:23.690 --> 05:27.140
This is a hands-on learning experience for you, so just be quiet and follow my lead!

05:28.660 --> 05:30.210
Then, Sensei, I have a question.

05:30.450 --> 05:31.260
What is it?

05:31.390 --> 05:32.840
Isn't there a no. 7?

05:33.150 --> 05:34.690
No. 7? What's that?

05:34.770 --> 05:36.130
This, of course.

05:40.270 --> 05:41.920
Not that, no that!

05:42.140 --> 05:44.480
Sensei only allows wholesome courtship!!

05:47.920 --> 05:50.050
It would be good if you just accepted that as well.

05:51.450 --> 05:54.090
Stop it! It's the middle of the afternoon!

05:54.160 --> 05:55.780
Bright is nice, right?

05:55.870 --> 05:57.260
Wai- Stop!

05:59.550 --> 06:01.370
Excuse me, parcel!

06:02.470 --> 06:03.820
Yes, yes, yes!!

06:03.900 --> 06:05.820
I'm coming right now!

06:12.540 --> 06:14.130
Usami Fuyuhiko?

06:14.570 --> 06:15.190
Who's that?

06:15.420 --> 06:18.540
Usami... meaning a relative of Usagi-san?

06:18.840 --> 06:20.090
Why is it addressed to me?

06:21.970 --> 06:24.310
A 4 SALMON BEAR!!

06:24.710 --> 06:25.710
What <i>is</i> this!?

06:25.240 --> 06:29.190
Thank you so much for your assistance the other day. You could call this a small token of thanks for the 3 salmon bear. I also had something a little
unusual at home and would be delighted if you would have it.
- Usami Fuyuhiko.

06:26.770 --> 06:29.250
<i>You could call this a small token of thanks for the 3 salmon bear.</i>

06:29.690 --> 06:32.160
<i>I also had something a little unusual at home.</i>

06:33.490 --> 06:35.080
Usagi's father!?

06:35.660 --> 06:38.300
By the way, how does he know of this address?

06:38.590 --> 06:39.960
Ohh!! Amazing!

06:40.540 --> 06:42.830
This is the first time I've seen a 4 salmon bear.

06:43.360 --> 06:44.580
Is this another one from Takahiro?

06:44.620 --> 06:46.570
Huh? No, wait! Don't look!

06:47.140 --> 06:49.110
Why are you so serious?

06:50.060 --> 06:52.390
Usami Fuyuhiko

06:54.270 --> 06:57.040
E-Er, it really was just a coincidence.

06:57.610 --> 07:02.100
He was worried about how to ride a train, so I just helped him.

07:02.380 --> 07:05.480
Do you remember, the 3 salmon bear Nii-chan gave?

07:05.570 --> 07:07.230
He took that off my hands for me.

07:07.310 --> 07:09.720
And after that he invited me for tea.

07:09.720 --> 07:12.130
Oh, I turned him down properly though.

07:13.060 --> 07:15.920
Then he offered to walk me to the exit.

07:16.120 --> 07:17.990
I thought that there's no harm in it.

07:18.460 --> 07:21.920
But then your brother was waiting near the exit to pick him up.

07:22.240 --> 07:24.550
That's how I found out that he's your father.

07:25.380 --> 07:26.550
Throw away this thing!

07:27.570 --> 07:31.380
Hey, hey! Don't throw it away! He was thoughtful enough to send it!

07:31.380 --> 07:32.770
Don't make me repeat myself.

07:33.380 --> 07:34.900
You let your guard down too much!

07:35.320 --> 07:36.200
Don't meet him again!

07:36.350 --> 07:38.980
Well, I said that it was a coincidence, didn't I?

07:39.210 --> 07:43.300
And anyway, that was sent to me! Don't throw it away as you please!

07:44.390 --> 07:46.060
You're acting strange!

07:46.190 --> 07:48.200
Would someone be this cautious normally?

07:48.280 --> 07:51.570
Don't say bad things about your family like this!

07:51.840 --> 07:52.350
What?

07:52.790 --> 07:54.590
U-Uh, no, um...

07:55.040 --> 07:59.790
I mean, I know this is not a place I should be sticking my nose into...

08:00.620 --> 08:05.600
<i>And I had told him a while back that I wouldn't ask him about his family until he felt like telling me himself.</i>

08:06.720 --> 08:09.260
Did you hear something from him?

08:09.540 --> 08:11.000
Eh? What?

08:12.510 --> 08:13.530
What is it?

08:13.970 --> 08:16.900
If you have something to say, just say it.

08:19.920 --> 08:20.950
<i>What's up?</i>

08:21.110 --> 08:22.080
<i>Just what is it?</i>

08:27.600 --> 08:29.730
Let's see, shopping's over.

08:30.450 --> 08:31.750
Next is the aquarium.

08:32.750 --> 08:34.460
Usagi-san, are you okay?

08:34.710 --> 08:35.970
Is this helping?

08:36.130 --> 08:37.800
Huh? Y-Yeah.

08:38.030 --> 08:40.100
Next was... the art museum, was it?

08:40.270 --> 08:42.510
I just said it was the aquarium.

08:42.580 --> 08:44.750
Huh? Oh, is that so?

08:45.760 --> 08:49.500
<i>What's up? Usagi-san has been really weird lately.</i>

08:50.160 --> 08:56.220
<i>Is me meeting his father and brother, even if it was just a coincidence, bothering him so much?</i>

08:57.590 --> 08:59.620
<i>Is it even worth bothering over?</i>

09:01.040 --> 09:04.670
<i>Oh, no. It might be something important to Usagi-san.</i>

09:05.910 --> 09:10.340
<i>For the time being, I should be careful not to make the atmosphere even more weirder.</i>

09:11.950 --> 09:14.380
Whoa! Awesome!!

09:15.940 --> 09:18.630
It's being a while since I saw these many fishes.

09:20.240 --> 09:24.200
Since this was an old building, I heard they rebuilt it entirely recently.

09:24.280 --> 09:28.860
When I looked at the entrance just now, there was this huge line. Good thing that we came early, right?

09:29.220 --> 09:32.440
Wow, wow! Awesome! So pretty!!

09:32.580 --> 09:35.310
Usagi-san, which fish are those large swarm over there?

09:35.430 --> 09:36.620
We ate some this morning, right?

09:37.710 --> 09:38.340
Horse mackerel?

09:38.740 --> 09:39.590
Horse mackerel indeed.

09:38.740 --> 09:42.000
*Joke: Sort of a play on words done in standup comedy- aji (horse mackerel) and maji (seriously)

09:39.830 --> 09:40.830
Seriously?

09:41.010 --> 09:42.620
Don't make lame *jokes.

09:43.580 --> 09:45.800
Oh, Usagi-san, the penguin exhibit!

09:45.880 --> 09:48.300
Let's look! There are supposed to be chicks right now!

09:48.510 --> 09:51.500
Yes, yes! Don't get so excited, sir! Those chicks won't run away.

09:51.570 --> 09:54.200
I-I'm not getting excited!

09:54.450 --> 09:57.130
Oh, mind if I go to the bathroom first?

09:57.540 --> 09:59.920
Then, I'll have a smoke in that sitting area.

09:59.980 --> 10:00.760
Okay.

10:09.420 --> 10:11.000
<i>Seems like his mood's fixed.</i>

10:11.840 --> 10:13.000
Oh, sorry.

10:15.960 --> 10:18.410
<i>Just why do I have to run into him with such a timing!?</i>

10:19.010 --> 10:20.640
Wait. I have something to say.

10:20.640 --> 10:21.940
I don't have anything.

10:21.940 --> 10:23.070
I do.

10:23.070 --> 10:24.400
Just let go of me!

10:24.400 --> 10:25.510
Please be quiet.

10:26.710 --> 10:28.300
Why are you in a place like this?

10:28.300 --> 10:31.870
F-For some fun, why else?

10:32.160 --> 10:34.620
And why are you here in a place like this?

10:34.980 --> 10:36.070
For work.

10:36.420 --> 10:38.350
I designed this.

10:40.480 --> 10:42.760
This is perfect timing. It's a message from my father.

10:42.940 --> 10:45.850
To thank you for helping him the other day, if the opportunity arises,

10:45.850 --> 10:49.640
he'd like to have dinner with you and wants to know when you have free time.

10:49.880 --> 10:50.370
Huh?

10:51.040 --> 10:54.270
Oh, that's right! I received his gift this morning.

10:54.460 --> 10:56.740
Please tell him, "Thank you very much", from me.

10:57.020 --> 10:59.490
So then, what about having dinner with him?

10:59.690 --> 11:02.550
Oh, no. Just the thought is enough.

11:02.630 --> 11:05.560
Between my part time job and classes, there's a lot going on.

11:05.560 --> 11:07.560
I understand. I'll relay that.

11:08.180 --> 11:09.680
Sorry for such an unreasonable request.

11:09.800 --> 11:13.410
It was my duty to relay this message, so I was obliged to ask.

11:14.730 --> 11:17.870
The gift that you mentioned- it was something worthless, wasn't it?

11:18.660 --> 11:22.420
If you don't want it, feel free to throw it away.

11:22.970 --> 11:24.810
<i>Somehow, this guy too...</i>

11:25.030 --> 11:27.420
It's just an old man's prank.

11:27.550 --> 11:28.920
I wish you'll forgive him.

11:29.010 --> 11:33.300
<i>Even though he's speaking of his father, his words are oddly barbed.</i>

11:33.970 --> 11:36.900
We don't get along too well...

11:37.480 --> 11:43.450
Um... maybe spending some frank, naked time, with floating rubber duckies would help you understand each other better.

11:44.260 --> 11:45.630
That's some lecturing.

11:45.950 --> 11:48.580
Would you normally ask something like that of me suddenly?

11:48.900 --> 11:52.920
Wrong! This is not about you and me!! Your father said so!!

11:54.190 --> 11:56.430
Ah... No... Um...

11:56.520 --> 12:00.270
I'm well aware that I'm in no place to speak like that.

12:00.390 --> 12:07.160
It's just that when your father was riding the train, he was worried over how to establish communication with you.

12:07.740 --> 12:10.290
Looked like he was thinking hard over things.

12:11.740 --> 12:14.090
I thought I'd atleast let you know the facts once.

12:14.440 --> 12:18.490
I thought maybe it wouldn't be so bad if you kept it somewhere in the back of your mind.

12:19.870 --> 12:22.940
Ah... well... it's none of my business.

12:24.320 --> 12:25.650
I finally understand.

12:25.870 --> 12:26.340
Huh?

12:27.280 --> 12:29.060
I also though a lot.

12:29.520 --> 12:36.490
I had thought that just like my relation to my father and brother, I thought about you too.

12:36.880 --> 12:37.660
Huh...

12:37.910 --> 12:40.310
But I've understood that it's not like that.

12:40.770 --> 12:41.500
Sorry?

12:42.410 --> 12:43.760
I love you.

12:46.230 --> 12:47.300
Hey, hey, hey, hey, hey!!!

12:47.400 --> 12:51.410
Get a hold of yourself! I'm a Japanese man, you know!

12:51.530 --> 12:53.480
Stop with the jokes!

12:53.670 --> 12:54.970
What do you want?

12:55.490 --> 12:59.020
I can provide you anything you desire.

12:59.290 --> 13:00.600
I humbly refuse.

13:00.750 --> 13:03.560
I think I've eaten a lifetime worth of strawberries and cherries.

13:03.700 --> 13:06.100
If you want to give me something, how about an island?

13:06.250 --> 13:06.970
An island, huh?

13:07.280 --> 13:09.020
If one in the south is okay...

13:09.360 --> 13:11.240
I don't want it! I don't want it!

13:13.890 --> 13:14.900
He's late.

13:19.380 --> 13:20.480
Hey, Misa-

13:21.760 --> 13:26.750
If you stay with Akihiko, it's clear that something unpleasant will happen to you eventually.

13:28.530 --> 13:29.220
What?

13:29.550 --> 13:33.270
Can a commoner like you withstand that kind of pressure?

13:33.460 --> 13:36.690
It might also cause trouble for your brother, you know.

13:37.240 --> 13:38.010
Just a-

13:38.150 --> 13:42.730
But if it's me, I can protect you from all such obstacles.

13:42.840 --> 13:45.340
Wait. Don't steer the conversation as you please.

13:45.430 --> 13:46.720
Let me make you realize.

13:47.030 --> 13:51.590
Even if you don't understand me right now, a day will definitely come when you choose me.

13:51.800 --> 13:52.960
It won't!

13:53.430 --> 13:56.360
I'm staying an Usagi-san's place of my own will.

13:56.500 --> 13:59.390
And I won't do anything that would cause trouble for my brother.

13:59.610 --> 14:03.490
It's okay as long as I don't cause Usagi-san any hardship, right?

14:21.430 --> 14:24.910
So? Think this little hands-on experiement will be useful?

14:25.280 --> 14:26.360
All thanks to you.

14:26.960 --> 14:28.890
I'll finish up the manuscript when we get home.

14:29.200 --> 14:30.570
You'd better do that.

14:30.710 --> 14:34.280
Just now, I received a worried message from Aikawa-san.
See?

14:34.730 --> 14:37.160
You really have no credibility with her.

14:37.420 --> 14:38.760
Everything is fine.

14:38.980 --> 14:41.370
Since Misaki taught me all these things.

14:41.840 --> 14:42.560
Hmm...

14:42.960 --> 14:46.300
Oh right, let me just say this, this is not just volunteering, you know.

14:46.390 --> 14:48.930
Oh, there's the Tokyo Tower!

14:49.710 --> 14:50.620
Misaki.

14:50.950 --> 14:51.540
Hm?

14:51.860 --> 14:55.600
I think it would be better if you don't concern yourself with me.

15:04.020 --> 15:06.840
O-Oh... that might be good.

15:07.280 --> 15:12.380
I mean, I got completely dragged into doing this hands-on lesson today, no matter how you think about it.

15:13.070 --> 15:18.260
And not just this time, somehow I always end up the victim of unfortunate circumstances whenever I'm with you.

15:19.510 --> 15:20.570
Right, right!

15:20.840 --> 15:23.750
Oh, a new volume of the manga I like is coming out.

15:23.750 --> 15:25.900
If you buy it for me, I'll forgive you.

15:26.150 --> 15:30.110
You could move into Takahiro's house, or you could live by yourself.

15:30.320 --> 15:33.460
No matter which one you choose, I'll bear the expenses.

15:34.460 --> 15:36.970
I don't want that.

15:38.710 --> 15:43.680
Oh, could it be, that you happened to see me with your brother at the aquarium?

15:44.690 --> 15:47.290
You know, I hope you believe me,

15:47.740 --> 15:50.910
we really just met by coincidence.

15:51.190 --> 15:58.510
Even today too, he told that he had come to the aquarium as a part of his business.

15:58.990 --> 16:04.960
Of course, I wouldn't have known any of that beforehand and so I couldn't be on my guard even if I wanted to.

16:05.070 --> 16:07.380
I mean, I'll still be on my guard from now on.

16:08.220 --> 16:09.240
Are you angry?

16:09.810 --> 16:12.280
No. It's not like that.

16:12.520 --> 16:13.800
Then what is it?

16:14.010 --> 16:15.780
You've been acting weird lately.

16:15.960 --> 16:17.940
Well, though you always act weird.

16:18.310 --> 16:22.270
<i>It can't be! Did I do something to cause trouble for Usagi-san?</i>

16:23.960 --> 16:27.710
I... don't want to hurt you.

16:28.460 --> 16:30.560
With regards to everything,

16:30.830 --> 16:36.640
rather than straining any relationship to a breaking point, I felt it was better to hold back and have lived that way.

16:37.370 --> 16:41.800
In fact, I thought I'd done pretty well for myself that way and was satisfied with it.

16:42.350 --> 16:47.350
But... ever since I've met you, I'm unable to stand it.

16:49.810 --> 16:54.400
In the future too, it is probably obvious that you'll come in contact with my family.

16:55.070 --> 16:57.870
My family knows the sides of me that you don't.

16:58.430 --> 17:04.660
If you find about it, I couldn't help but think that you would want to go away from me then.

17:05.040 --> 17:08.940
If that happens, I'd do anything to stop you.

17:09.610 --> 17:10.760
I'm worried.

17:11.290 --> 17:16.000
There's a part of me that doesn't want to restrain you, but also a part that wants to lock you up.

17:16.800 --> 17:19.370
Hurting you is the one thing that I don't want to do.

17:19.760 --> 17:21.670
But reality isn't like that.

17:21.890 --> 17:25.920
I'd rather we part ways right now, than have you despise me and leave me one day.

17:26.700 --> 17:30.620
The one thing I fear most is losing you.

17:36.460 --> 17:41.480
No... I mean... it's not like you've done anything to hurt (me).

17:42.150 --> 17:45.710
The moment we started living together, I forced myself on you.

17:47.860 --> 17:50.640
Uh... Um... then... is it...

17:51.090 --> 17:57.860
Then, the reason you've be acting this weird lately is all... my fault, is it?

17:58.940 --> 18:00.250
<i>I understood for the first time.</i>

18:01.110 --> 18:03.610
<i>That Usagi-san was worried about something like this.</i>

18:04.010 --> 18:07.960
<i>Is it okay to think that he doesn't want me to hate him?</i>

18:10.150 --> 18:14.890
<i>The one who got the wrong idea was me, the one who didn't understand was me.</i>

18:15.530 --> 18:17.790
<i>Usagi-san was always worried.</i>

18:18.150 --> 18:21.280
<i>He was always, always thinking about me.</i>

18:21.720 --> 18:22.510
<i>Sorry.</i>

18:23.040 --> 18:26.630
<i>I'm not very good with complicated things or big words, but...</i>

18:26.940 --> 18:29.120
The one thing that I must say

18:28.070 --> 18:29.050
Usagi-san,

18:31.240 --> 18:32.370
It's okay.

18:33.100 --> 18:36.880
I... love you.

18:41.800 --> 18:43.150
Anyway!

18:44.260 --> 18:47.690
What was that? So <i>that's</i> what this all was about, eh?

18:47.810 --> 18:50.420
Keeping all those worthless worries bottled up.

18:50.800 --> 18:52.370
I was worried for nothing!

18:53.290 --> 18:54.710
It's not worthless.

18:56.740 --> 18:59.130
I know that.

19:01.370 --> 19:04.540
You know, I'm really alright with it.

19:04.970 --> 19:06.880
It's not like... I was forced.

19:07.160 --> 19:10.320
Besides, only when you mentioned it, I thought, "oh that's what it was about, huh?".

19:11.120 --> 19:14.000
If I really disliked it, I wouldn't have stayed with you.

19:18.170 --> 19:21.690
Wh-What? Say something!

19:22.850 --> 19:24.260
Speak up!

19:25.500 --> 19:31.010
<i>Usagi-san wouldn't say a word, wouldn't look at me and just kept gazing out of the window.</i>

19:32.050 --> 19:34.420
<i>It's been a while since we held hands.</i>

19:34.810 --> 19:41.050
<i>Come to think of it, Usagi-san's hands are supposed to be cold, but right now, they are very warm.</i>

19:41.830 --> 19:44.930
<i>I wonder why, is it because it's closest to my heart?</i>

19:45.730 --> 19:52.850
<i>Though I think it can't really be relayed, but I wonder whose beat is flowing in through my hand to my heart.</i>

19:53.440 --> 19:56.270
<i>Whose pulse is this?</i>

20:08.220 --> 20:09.300
Our clothes at least...

20:16.200 --> 20:17.180
I love you.

20:46.790 --> 20:51.930
Yokogiru dake wa ichinichi no owari ni

20:46.790 --> 20:51.930
Crossing paths at the end of the day,

20:52.060 --> 20:57.320
itsu kara ka kimi ga sakimawari shite matte ite

20:52.060 --> 20:57.320
at some point you went up ahead and waited for me.

20:57.670 --> 21:02.690
ureshii kimochi bai ni shite kurete

20:57.670 --> 21:02.690
You doubled all my happiness,

21:02.690 --> 21:09.380
kanamishi kimochi hanbun ni shite kureru kara

21:02.690 --> 21:09.380
and halved all my sadness.

21:09.490 --> 21:14.490
kore kara donna michi aruitemo

21:09.490 --> 21:14.490
No matter what path I walk in the future,

21:14.890 --> 21:19.170
kitto sore wa kimi he to tsuzuiteru

21:14.890 --> 21:19.170
will surely lead to you.

21:19.170 --> 21:21.930
boku no saki ni wa kimi ga ite

21:19.170 --> 21:21.930
You're there up ahead of me,

21:21.930 --> 21:24.790
kimi no saki ni wa boka ga iru

21:21.930 --> 21:24.790
I'm there ahead of you,

21:24.790 --> 21:30.060
hoka no dare mo inai futari dake no basho

21:24.790 --> 21:30.060
A place for just the two of us with no one else around.

21:30.060 --> 21:35.960
sore ga boku no subete nanda sore ga boku wo karuku shiteru na

21:30.060 --> 21:35.960
That's my everything, and lifts the weight off my shoulders.

21:36.550 --> 21:41.030
mou doko he mo ikanaide

21:36.550 --> 21:41.030
Hey, don't go anywhere.

21:41.030 --> 21:46.490
yakusoku no basho wa itsumo hidamari no kaori wo sasete

21:41.030 --> 21:46.490
Our promised place always has the smell of sunshine.

21:46.490 --> 21:51.880
boku no ashimoto wo terashiteirunda

21:46.490 --> 21:51.880
It's casting a light at my feet.

21:51.880 --> 21:57.700
kimi no koto ga suki da yotte to ieru boku ga suki dakara

21:51.880 --> 21:57.700
I love myself being able to say "I love you!"

21:58.090 --> 22:03.380
mune no oku de sotto arigatou

21:58.090 --> 22:03.380
Softly in my heart I say, "Thank you."

22:07.230 --> 22:10.240
Why am I in a place like this?

22:10.400 --> 22:11.460
Oh, that's right.

22:11.880 --> 22:14.420
Yesterday, we came here on our way back from the Ferris wheel...

22:15.800 --> 22:18.030
I love you.

22:22.270 --> 22:24.440
What was all that? What just happened?

22:24.510 --> 22:26.760
I got caught up in the moment, didn't I?

22:26.850 --> 22:29.470
Well, you know, there are times like that too!

22:30.400 --> 22:33.790
<i>But, saying "I love you" is pretty easy, isn't it?</i>

22:34.870 --> 22:38.060
<i>Though, it's good to see that Usagi-san seems reassured.</i>

22:42.240 --> 22:46.710
Went out to
buy some cigarettes

22:42.530 --> 22:46.190
Says, Usagi-san went out to buy some cigarettes.. Hmm? A letter?

22:48.130 --> 22:49.950
No, this is a novel.

22:50.050 --> 22:52.110
Did he finish the one he was stuck on?

22:52.990 --> 22:54.260
the gentle sound of his voice

22:54.260 --> 22:55.260
of the kiss a moment before

22:55.260 --> 22:57.100
embraced each other in the shower.

22:58.510 --> 22:59.710
You're awake, huh?

22:59.960 --> 23:04.320
Honarable Sir Usami, please excuse me, but what might this be?

23:04.610 --> 23:06.120
My new boys' love novel.

23:06.550 --> 23:09.820
What the hell happened with the "novel of youth" I gave you my full cooperation for!!?

23:11.060 --> 23:13.470
Now that you mention it, there was something like that.

23:15.940 --> 23:16.630
Yes.

23:16.760 --> 23:17.870
I'm going for a walk.

23:17.870 --> 23:19.140
Hey wait, will you!!

23:19.170 --> 23:21.810
Misaki-kun, where is Sensei? The manuscript is ready, right?

23:21.810 --> 23:24.540
The printers say they want the manuscript before the deadline no matter what!

23:24.540 --> 23:26.060
Wha! Whaaat!!?

23:26.160 --> 23:27.840
Wait up, rotten Usagi!

23:27.940 --> 23:30.480
Like I said, don't drag me into things!!!

23:31.780 --> 23:34.450
<i>Nii-chan, I'm coming home very very soon.</i>

23:35.430 --> 23:44.670
Raws: BDRIP (from nyaa.se)
Translation: aarinfantasy
Timing, Typesetting, Minor script editing and Encoding: asckj1

23:57.020 --> 23:59.990
Marriage is made in heaven
